## 3. Database ER Diagram & Schema Design

### Entity Relationship Diagram (Mermaid)

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USERS ||--o{ TICKETS : "creates (user_id)"
    USERS ||--o{ TICKETS : "assigned to (assigned_to)"
    USERS ||--o{ TICKET_COMMENTS : "posts (user_id)"
    TICKETS ||--o{ TICKET_COMMENTS : "has (ticket_id)"

    USERS {
        int id PK
        string name
        string email UK
        string password_hash
        enum role "customer | agent"
        datetime created_at
    }

    TICKETS {
        int id PK
        int user_id FK
        string subject
        text description
        enum priority "low | medium | high"
        enum status "open | in_progress | closed"
        int assigned_to FK "nullable"
        datetime created_at
        datetime updated_at
    }

    TICKET_COMMENTS {
        int id PK
        int ticket_id FK
        int user_id FK
        text comment
        datetime created_at
    }
```

### Table Definitions
1. **`users`**:
   - `id`: INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY
   - `name`: VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
   - `email`: VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL UNIQUE
   - `password_hash`: VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
   - `role`: ENUM('customer', 'agent') DEFAULT 'customer'
   - `created_at`: TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP

2. **`tickets`**:
   - `id`: INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY
   - `user_id`: INT NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY -> users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
   - `subject`: VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
   - `description`: TEXT NOT NULL
   - `priority`: ENUM('low', 'medium', 'high') DEFAULT 'medium'
   - `status`: ENUM('open', 'in_progress', 'closed') DEFAULT 'open'
   - `assigned_to`: INT NULLABLE, FOREIGN KEY -> users(id) ON DELETE SET NULL
   - `created_at`: TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
   - `updated_at`: TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
   - **Indexes**: `idx_tickets_status (status)`, `idx_tickets_user_id (user_id)`, `idx_tickets_assigned_to (assigned_to)`

3. **`ticket_comments`**:
   - `id`: INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY
   - `ticket_id`: INT NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY -> tickets(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
   - `user_id`: INT NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY -> users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
   - `comment`: TEXT NOT NULL
   - `created_at`: TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
   - **Indexes**: `idx_comments_ticket_id (ticket_id)`

